  "id": "5a989192-864e-5e62-b57b-1f09046d7d39",
  "slug": "atlantic-beach-pie-recipe-8685509",
  "name": "Atlantic Beach Pie",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "A beachside favorite turned Southern classic, this Atlantic Beach Pie recipe crosses key lime pie and lemon meringue pie for a uniquely refreshing treat. The saltine cracker crust gives the pie a salty-sweet flavor and irresistible texture. Here's how to make Atlantic Beach Pie.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Gather all ingredients."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Crush saltines so that they resemble coarse meal. Stir crushed crackers, melted butter, sugar, and egg white together in a medium bowl until combined."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Transfer mixture to a 9-inch glass or ceramic standard pie plate greased with cooking spray; firmly press on bottom and up the sides. Freeze for 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until crust is lightly browned, 15 to 20 minutes. Transfer to a wire rack; cool slightly, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "While crust cools, whisk condensed milk and egg yolks together until smooth. Zest 1 of the lemons and 1 of the limes to yield 1 teaspoon each. Juice zested lemon and 2 of the limes to yield 1/4 cup juice each. Whisk lime juice, lemon juice, and 1 teaspoon of the vanilla into condensed milk mixture until smooth. Pour mixture into warm crust."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Bake at 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) until center is just set, about 15 minutes. Transfer to a wire rack; cool 1 hour at room temperature. Refrigerate, uncovered, until thoroughly chilled, at least 2 hours."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "When ready to serve, beat cream, powdered sugar, and remaining 1 teaspoon vanilla in a large bowl with an electric mixer on high speed until stiff peaks form, about 2 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Spread whipped cream topping over chilled pie, leaving about a 1/2-inch border of custard showing around crust. Thinly slice remaining lemon and lime into rounds. Twist slices and arrange decoratively over whipped cream. Sprinkle with reserved lemon and lime zest."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "Enjoy! Recipe developed by Julia Levy"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
